            <ArticleTitle>Coelioscopic cholecystectomy. Preliminary report of 36 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>60-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intra-abdominal endoscopy, routinely used for gynecologic operations can be extended safely for cholecystectomy in uncomplicated cholelithiasis. Thirty-six patients underwent coelioscopic cholecystectomy with few and only benign complications. The main advantages are cosmetic preservation, reduction of postoperative pain, shortening of hospital stay, and early recovery of a normal activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
